<title>SWITZERLAND: Paper says Swissair wants A330-200s.</title>
<headline>Paper says Swissair wants A330-200s.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Swiss newspaper reported that Swissair AG's management would propose to the board of directors' meeting this week purchasing Airbus A330-200 jets to replace its A310-300 fleet.</p>
<p>An airline spokesman said he could not confirm the unsourced report by the Neue Zuercher Zeitung.</p>
<p>&quot;It is clear we expect a decision on replacing our A310 aircraft, but at the moment two types are in the foreground -- the A330s and Boeing 767s,&quot; he said in response to an inquiry.</p>
</text>
